# Caddy as the public entrypoint and API load balancer.
#
# - Terminates TLS (auto Let's Encrypt for a real domain; see the commented
#   block) and forwards browser + agent traffic to the API replicas.
# - Active health checks hit /api/readyz, so a replica that is draining for
#   shutdown or has lost a dependency is taken out of rotation automatically.
# - WebSocket upgrades (agents dial /agents/connect) are proxied transparently.
# - /internal/* is the private inter-replica dispatch API and must never be
#   reachable from outside; it is refused here and only used replica-to-replica
#   on the compose network.
#
# Replace :80 with your domain (e.g. duckhaven.example.com) to enable auto-TLS,
# and set COOKIE_SECURE=true + OIDC_REDIRECT_BASE_URL accordingly.

:80 {
	@internal path /internal/*
	respond @internal 404

	reverse_proxy api-1:8000 api-2:8000 {
		lb_policy round_robin
		health_uri /api/readyz
		health_interval 5s
		health_timeout 2s
	}
}
